%I A401225 #4 Oct 24 2026 16:50:40
%S A401225 4,44,350,3004,24706,193406,1346758,8650416,52128242,299349210,
%T A401225 1653637492,8828301226,45743165894,230934909328,1139486126866,
%U A401225 5510071794736
%N A401225 Number of sets S of n+6 points of the 5 X n grid such that any two distinct rectangles with all four corners at grid points (tilted rectangles included) have distinct sets of corners outside S.
%C A401225 Sets are counted as subsets of the grid, not up to symmetry.
%C A401225 No such set exists for n < 8. For n >= 8, n+6 is the largest possible size (see A397315), so a(n) = A399580(5,n).
%C A401225 Every such set has six columns with two points each and one point in every other column, and the six row pairs are the edges of a complete bipartite graph K_{2,3} on the five rows.
%C A401225 The g.f. is rational (see the Pemmasani link), but it is not known.
%C A401225 a(8)-a(12) were computed by two independent programs, and a(13)-a(23) by two exact transfer counters (see the Pemmasani link).
%H A401225 Peter Kagey, <a href="https://peterkagey.com/problems/001/">Open Problem Collection, Problem 001</a>.
%H A401225 Arjun Pemmasani, <a href="https://github.com/apemm/Kagey-Problems/blob/main/kagey-problems/problem001/jis/pemmasani.pdf">Maximum Blackouts That Keep Every Lattice Rectangle Identifiable</a>, preprint, 2026.
%H A401225 Arjun Pemmasani, <a href="https://github.com/apemm/Kagey-Problems/tree/main/kagey-problems/problem001">Solvers, exhaustive verification, and pre-registration ledger for Problem 001</a> (GitHub repository).
%e A401225 a(8) = 4. The four sets are the images of the set below under the reflection in the middle row and the reversal of the columns (1 = in S, rows numbered from the top):
%e A401225   1 0 0 0 0 0 0 1
%e A401225   0 0 1 0 0 0 1 1
%e A401225   0 0 0 0 0 1 1 0
%e A401225   1 1 0 0 0 1 0 0
%e A401225   0 1 1 1 1 0 0 0
%Y A401225 Row 5 of A399580 for n >= 8.
%Y A401225 Cf. A397315, A401223, A401224.
%K A401225 nonn,more,new
%O A401225 8,1
%A A401225 _Arjun Pemmasani_, Oct 18 2026
